  "id": "u13-l01",
  "unit": "u13-requests",
  "title": "Come here, sit down",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**A তুমি command is just the তুমি present form.** You already know it: **খাও** 'eat!', **যাও** 'go!', **দাও** 'give!', **করো** 'do!'. The same goes for any verb: **বসো** 'sit', **বলো** 'say', **শোনো** 'listen', **দেখো** 'look', **নাও** 'take'.\n\nOne is irregular: **আসা** 'come' → **এসো** (many Bangladeshis say **আসো**). **এদিকে এসো** 'Come here (this way)'.\n\nUse these with friends, younger relatives and children, people you call **তুমি**. Add **একটু** 'a little' to soften: **একটু শোনো** 'listen a sec'. The sentence often needs no 'you': **এখানে বসো** 'Sit here'.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "bosho",
      "bn": "বসো",
      "tr": "bosho",
      "en": "sit (familiar)",
      "notes": "তুমি command of বসা; same form as তুমি বসো 'you sit'."
    },
    {
      "id": "esho",
      "bn": "এসো",
      "tr": "esho",
      "en": "come (familiar)",
      "notes": "Irregular: আসা → এসো. Many Bangladeshi speakers say আসো (asho); both are accepted in typed answers."
    },
    {
      "id": "bolo",
      "bn": "বলো",
      "tr": "bolo",
      "en": "say (familiar)",
      "notes": "Same form as তুমি বলো 'you say'."
    },
    {
      "id": "shono",
      "bn": "শোনো",
      "tr": "shono",
      "en": "listen (familiar)",
      "notes": "Also gets a friend's attention: শোনো! 'Listen!'"
    },
    {
      "id": "dekho",
      "bn": "দেখো",
      "tr": "dekho",
      "en": "look (familiar)",
      "notes": "Same form as তুমি দেখো 'you see'."
    },
    {
      "id": "nao",
      "bn": "নাও",
      "tr": "nao",
      "en": "take (familiar)",
      "notes": "Offering something: এটা নাও 'Take this / Here you go'."
    },
    {
